                        ],
                        "form": "rosins"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a5bca422-1d75-362a-8960-e73a4bb3a758",
                        "entry_id": "618eb879-9a02-3c4f-8cce-a1eb1694c04c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A solid form of resin, obtained from liquid resin by vaporizing its volatile components."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a6727a5-c6a7-4d2e-b1da-2e7f02e61ce1",
                                "sense_id": "a5bca422-1d75-362a-8960-e73a4bb3a758",
                                "text": "The action of the bow therefore depends almost entirely upon the application of rosin and upon its frictional properties. Violin rosin is a natural gum obtained from conifers such as larch that produce turpentine."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a957e45a-01b9-310b-964a-3307193f6d23",
                        "entry_id": "618eb879-9a02-3c4f-8cce-a1eb1694c04c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Resin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ebebf90-b0fc-4f89-b196-a434b8060b6b",
                                "sense_id": "a957e45a-01b9-310b-964a-3307193f6d23",
                                "text": "‘It is delicate,’ said Pansa, ‘but there is perhaps the least particle too much of rosin in its flavor.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e48df3a9-1364-48f4-8d61-500b54f2c7f2",
                                "sense_id": "a957e45a-01b9-310b-964a-3307193f6d23",
                                "text": "From three o'clock onward they would be burning rosin and pitch pine (the sign of preparation), and so one had the picturesque spectacle of a rank, some two or three miles long, of tall, ascending columns of coal-black smoke; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbf7c9c3-cc83-4a9c-8b1e-bba530471abf",
                                "sense_id": "a957e45a-01b9-310b-964a-3307193f6d23",
                                "text": "A thick, fat smoke oozed out from the fire, and a heavy smell of burned rosin and singed hair filled the air."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
